{
 "description": "Hand-labelled up axis for STL pose evaluation. Labelled by eye from 6-tile up-candidate contact sheets. Models whose upright is genuinely undefined (loose hands, wings, swords, pipes, pins) were excluded.",
 "history": [
  "2026-09-09: five labels pointed at DM Stash `75_Unsupported_*` files, which the walk's anchored `^75_` rule stopped indexing (commit ea1ef04), so they had silently left the measurable set. Four were re-pointed at their `32_` twins — verified the same mesh at a different scale: identical vertex counts, identical scale-normalised bounding boxes, identical geometry pick, and a contact sheet that reads the same, so the axis carries over unchanged. The fifth, 75_Unsupported_Wajoski_Wolf2, was dropped rather than re-pointed: its `32_` twin was already labelled here, so `orig` had been carrying the same wolf twice (vertex counts differ by 27 of 2.7M) and every pooled figure quoted on 44 models was really 43 distinct ones.",
  "2026-09-09: two `expand` labels were withdrawn after review as parts rather than models. `Apprentice_Grimoire_L` is one of 31 interchangeable hand options in a modular wizard's directory, beside `Apprentice_Dagger_R` and `Apprentice_Grimoire_R`; it carries the `_L` marker `pose_label_expand.LIKELY_PART` matches, and only reached a sheet because seeds 909 and 5150 were drawn before that filter existed. `32mm_OdDracnesThrone_B` is the one no naming rule can see: it is one of A/B/C/D that assemble into a single throne, and its `_B` is a component letter, not a left/right marker. What identifies it is the directory, not the name. A lettered-family sweep over the whole set found no third case.",
  "2026-09-09: `sprue` joined the walk's NON_MODEL_TAGS — a sprue is the packing, a raft carrying several pieces (or five of one) that the same directory already indexes individually. That cut `Damaged Metal Sheet Sprue` from the holdout, which is why it is no longer here. tests/test_naming.py::test_no_labelled_model_is_cut_by_the_vocabulary now fails whenever a vocabulary change orphans a label, so this class of silent shrink cannot recur."
 ],
 "axes": [
  "+Z",
  "-Z",
  "+Y",
  "-Y",
  "+X",
  "-X"
 ],
 "sets": {
  "orig": "first 40-model random sample; probes and the min-max scheme were tuned against these, so numbers on this set are optimistic",
  "holdout": "fresh sample from files the first never touched; method frozen",
  "hard": "models added by hand, chosen for being failure-prone rather than by random draw. Deliberately selected, so accuracy on this set is not comparable to orig/holdout and must not be pooled into a headline number without saying so.",
  "expand": "random draw from the collection walk, seed 909, 5150, excluding every path already labelled; proposed by a labeller measured on the first 49 and confirmed by hand from the same six-tile sheets — so these are model-proposed and human-confirmed, not hand-labelled the way orig/holdout were. Drawn without the likely-part filter, so it is a sample of the collection rather than of its whole models. Method frozen as of this draw.",
  "expand2": "random draw from the collection walk, seed 7777, excluding every path already labelled, and every name carrying a left/right marker or a lettered-family sibling — so this set is a sample of the collection's *whole* models, not of the collection, and its rates are not comparable to `expand`'s. Differs from `expand` in one more way that matters: there the human decided part-vs-model first and the labeller only proposed axes; here the labeller proposed **both**, and the human adjudicated both on their own review pages. Agreement on that review: 62/66 on part-vs-model and 36/38 on the axis, with every disagreement but one falling inside the proposals the labeller had flagged as uncertain. Method frozen as of this draw.",
  "reclaim": "the 16 models the 2026-09-09 part triage wrongly cut as parts, recovered by the 2026-09-10 class pass which ruled they are not parts at all — terrain, furniture and one figure with ordinary uprights. NOT a sample of anything: it is the error set of an earlier filter, so it is biased toward shapes that fooled that filter (flat slabs, lettered families, near-symmetric solids). Proposed by a labeller and confirmed by hand from the same six-tile sheets; 3 were ruled to have no defensible upright."
 },
